From 466954390d8d382da9f250bba2393d07261a32e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "servicemp3 gst-1.26 review" <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:17:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] servicemp3: detect HLS/DASH reliably, also with query
 strings

The source type was derived from strrchr(filename, '.'). For typical
IPTV URLs such as http://host/live/stream.m3u8?token=abc the "extension"
became ".m3u8?token=abc", so is_hls stayed FALSE: no connection-speed
hint, and - if the service reference enables buffering - the
pause/resume-on-0%/100% logic, which is deliberately skipped for
adaptive streams, was applied to HLS.

- getTypeExtension(): ignore query string/fragment for URLs and any
  dot that belongs to a directory component. Unit-tested on ten
  URL/path forms (old: 6 misclassified, new: 0).
- Recognise ".mpd" as DASH (is_dash) and treat it like HLS.
- Connect playbin "deep-element-added" for streaming sources and flag
  the stream as adaptive when a hlsdemux*/dashdemux*/mssdemux* element
  is plugged. This covers URLs without a telling extension. The
  handler runs in a streaming thread and therefore only uses atomics
  and thread safe GObject calls.
- The BUFFERING handler now uses isAdaptiveStream().

Background (verified with GStreamer 1.26.11): playbin's decodebin is
not streams-aware, so hlsdemux2/dashdemux2/mssdemux2 (adaptivedemux2)
always fail with "Element requires a streams-aware context" and the
classic hlsdemux/dashdemux/mssdemux from gst-plugins-bad do the work.
Their names start with the same prefixes and are matched here.

Note: a URL such as http://host/get?file=a.m3u8 (dot only in the query)
is no longer taken as HLS by extension; it is caught by the
deep-element-added path once hlsdemux is plugged.
---
 servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 servicemp3/servicemp3.h   |  7 ++-
 2 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp b/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
index 8ac881c..fe6d052 100644
--- a/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
+++ b/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
@@ -62,6 +62,27 @@ typedef enum
 	GST_PLAY_FLAG_FORCE_FILTERS = (1 << 11),
 } GstPlayFlags;
 
+/*
+ * Return the file extension (including the dot) used to classify a source.
+ * For URLs a query string or fragment is ignored, so that
+ * "http://host/live/stream.m3u8?token=abc" is recognised as ".m3u8".
+ */
+static std::string getTypeExtension(const char *filename)
+{
+	std::string path(filename);
+	if (path.find("://") != std::string::npos)
+	{
+		size_t q = path.find_first_of("?#");
+		if (q != std::string::npos)
+			path.erase(q);
+	}
+	size_t slash = path.find_last_of('/');
+	size_t dot = path.find_last_of('.');
+	if (dot == std::string::npos || (slash != std::string::npos && dot < slash))
+		return "";
+	return path.substr(dot);
+}
